WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.830 align:start position:0%
 
is  dear friends i'm delighted to be with  you  and it is fitting that we start this new  year with  a one planet summit in paris talking  about biodiversity  because i believe 2021 will be the year  when the world turns over new leaf for  our planet  in a few months we the world will come  together in kunming  and this cup 15 for nature  must be like the cup 21 was for climate  and we need a paris style agreement to  go with it  global and game-changing  the stakes could not be higher and the  imperative  act could not be more compelling this is  about sustainable development  because thriving biodiversity can ensure  access to food water and energy  for billions of people this is about  equality  because we know that the effects of  nature loss  disproportionately affect poorer  and indigenous communities  this is about our security because  conflicts explode when more people  grapple  for less natural resources  and this is about our quality of life  because we need nature in our lives for  our physical and mental health  we all know the scale and the urgency of  the task ahead of us  this year and we see the changes in our  everyday lives  from more concrete blocks to less  wilderness and wildlife  to increasing temperatures and extreme  weather  and these worrying changes are different  sides of the same coin  in fact they mutually reinforce each  other  when we lose forests we don't just  lose green space or natural habitat  we lose a key ally in our fight against  climate change  when temperatures rise and nature  disappears  we suffer more natural disasters and  zoonotic diseases  we have spoken a lot about these links  between biodiversity loss and covet  but this is not the first last or  even most telling example think of how  one of the  deadliest outbreaks of ebola is thought  to have started with a young boy playing  next to a tree in a remote village in  guinea  a tree that had been infested by bats  who had been pushed towards the village  because 80 percent of forests in the  region had been destroyed  and we know the tragic repercussions  this had  and if we don't urgently act to protect  our nature  we may already be at the beginning of an  era  of pandemics but we can do something  about it  it needs concerted global action local  sustainable development  and just as we cooperate for our one  planet  we need each other for our one health  and this is why we will prioritize  research on one health  across horizon europe and let me be  clear  we will invest several hundred million  euros  over the next four years for research  on biodiversity animal health  emerging diseases and much more  it is why we will work closely with our  international partners on  research in the spirit of the preside  initiative launched by france and member  states  which the european commission welcomes  and it is also why we will bolster and  sponsor initiatives like the african-led  great green wall  i would like to congratulate the african  union and all  of the partners involved for bringing  a decades-old dream to life  we have already seen the difference it  can make stretching from senegal in the  west to  debut in the east it has helped restore  15 million hectares of degraded land in  ethiopia  and supported farmers in niger to  produce enough grain to feed an extra  2.5 million people a year  and this is why i say today we will  mobilize  even more than the 700 million euros per  year  already raised for the great green wall  project  the more partners and the more member  states join and invest  the more we can do and this is the  spirit of team europe and i am  determined that we can do so much more  working with our african partners  this shows that turning over a new leaf  for nature all comes down to local  action  and global ambition this is why the  european green deal  we are stepping up own action and  ambition both  locally and globally our new  biodiversity  and farm to fork strategies will lead  the way  they set out the eu's ambitions to  protect indeed 30 percent of land and  sea areas  in europe and around the world  they will help us restore damaged rivers  and plant three billion trees by 2030.  will bring help and bring back to  pollinators  to agriculture lands and reduce the use  and risk of harmful pesticides  and the new greener common agricultural  policy  will help us protect livelihoods and  food security  while we protect our nature and our  climate  but we know we need to do more being a  major economy  and a trading superpower comes  with responsibilities and it is our duty  to ensure  that our single market does not  drive deforestation in local communities  in other parts of the world  and this is why later this year  we will propose new legislation  to minimize the risk of products linked  to global deforestation  being placed on the european market  so europe is ready to lead the way and i  hope others will join us in that effort  dear friends this sums up the eu's  approach  in this historic year for nature  we will lead by ambition and action  at home and we will do everything we can  to bring  as many partners on board with us  this is why we will work to broker an  ambitious agreement in kunming  and it is why we will support  initiatives like the great green wall  let's make sure that we turn over this  new leaf together thanks very much  to all the participants and thanks very  much to you mr president sherry manuel  merci beaucoup  [Music]  african  [Music]  you

